You are a senior Laravel engineer. We are building "Yuppy AI Photobook Designer" on the TALL stack (Tailwind, Alpine.js, Laravel, Livewire 3). This is PHASE 1 ONLY: Foundation & Architecture. Do not build AI, uploads of photographs, the editor, renderer, orders or payments.

STEP 0 - Inspect first
Inspect the repository and environment (PHP, Composer, Node, MySQL). If no Laravel app exists, create one (Laravel 11 or the compatible version). Summarise what you found and your plan in /docs/architecture.md before writing feature code.

STEP 1 - Setup
- Livewire 3, Alpine.js, Tailwind CSS via Vite, MySQL.
- Laravel Breeze with the Livewire (Volt) stack for auth: register, login, logout, password reset, email verification.
- Pest for tests, Laravel Pint, Larastan (level 5).
- Queue driver: database. Filesystem: private disk for all user files.
- Self-hosted fonts: one elegant serif for headings, one clean sans for body.
- Do not install Konva, Fabric or any editor library yet.

STEP 2 - Roles
- users.role enum: admin, photographer, customer. Plus status and last_login_at.
- Customers and photographers may self-register (role chosen at registration, admin cannot be self-registered). Admins are seeded.
- Role middleware and Laravel policies. No role logic scattered in views.

STEP 3 - Database
Create migrations, models, factories and relationships with proper foreign keys and indexes for: users, photographer_profiles, customers, branding_profiles, occasions, design_families, book_formats, manufacturer_templates, photobook_projects (stub), ai_requests (empty), audit_logs.
manufacturer_templates must have nullable measurement columns and is_verified=false by default. NEVER seed or invent manufacturer measurements.
photobook_projects: owner_type (yuppy|photographer|customer), photographer_profile_id nullable, customer_id nullable, branding_mode, occasion_id, book_format_id, title, status, soft deletes.

STEP 4 - Authorisation (critical)
- Policies: PhotographerProfile, BrandingProfile, Customer, PhotobookProject.
- Photographers can only access their own records. Customers only their own. Admin all.
- Lists must be owner-filtered by default.
- A photographer-owned project must never resolve Yuppy branding. Implement a BrandingResolver service with this rule and test it.
- Files (logos) are stored privately and served only through authenticated, policy-checked routes.

STEP 5 - Features
- Role-based dashboards: admin, photographer, customer, sharing one app shell (sidebar + top bar, responsive, collapsible on mobile).
- Photographer: studio profile + branding profile form (studio name, phone, email, optional website, socials, logo upload with validation: image types only, size limit, no SVG with scripts).
- Admin: manage Yuppy branding profile; list photographers and customers (read-only for now).
- AuditLogger service; log login, logout, profile and branding changes.

STEP 6 - UI
Design tokens in tailwind.config: charcoal, black, warm ivory, champagne gold (accent only), neutral greys. Serif headings, sans body, generous whitespace. Build reusable Blade/Livewire components: card, button variants, input, select, file upload, modal, toast, badge, empty state. Premium creative-studio feel, not a generic admin template. No heavy gradients, no unnecessary animation.

STEP 7 - Seeders
Admin user, 2 photographers (each with branding), 2 customers, 8 occasions (Wedding, Engagement, Graduation, Birthday, Family, Travel, Corporate Portfolio, Baby/Newborn), 5 design families (Story, Minimal, Moments, Cinematic, Signature), 6 book formats (8x10 P, 8x12 P, 12x8 L, 10x12 P, 12x12 Square, 12x18 P), Yuppy branding profile with placeholder logo. Occasions and families must be data, not hard-coded in views.

STEP 8 - Tests (Pest)
- Each role lands on its own dashboard.
- Customer gets 403 on admin and photographer routes.
- Photographer A cannot view, edit, list or download Photographer B's profile, branding, customers, projects or logo.
- Logo upload rejects invalid type and oversize files.
- BrandingResolver: photographer project never returns Yuppy branding.
- Seeders produce 8 occasions, 5 families, 6 formats, and zero verified manufacturer templates.
- Audit entries are written for login and profile changes.

STEP 9 - Docs
Write /docs/architecture.md, /docs/roadmap.md (10 phases) and /docs/phase-1.md (how to run, test, and what is next).

